# Migration-narrowing gate allowlist.
#
# Format: CHECK_A|<rust_file>|<NAME>|<python_file>  # reason: <why this
# is a coincidental name collision, not a real capability narrowing>
#
# Every entry MUST carry a written reason and MUST be a coincidental
# name/identifier collision, not a real defect. Do NOT allowlist a genuine
# capability-narrowing defect (a Rust port silently dropping a
# parameter/precision the Python had) — that is the exact defect class this
# gate exists to catch. See scripts/check_migration_narrowing.py module
# docstring for the two seeded historical instances (H_CONV_BACKGROUND,
# escape_via.rs rotation).
#
# Seeded 2026-08-07 from a real `--init` run against origin/main
# (63ec4e756). At seed time this run additionally surfaced two more, not
# previously catalogued, live instances of the same defect class
# (net_ordering.rs `rotation` and terminal_planning.rs `initial_rotation`,
# both `Option<i64>` mirroring `float(comp.initial_rotation) * math.pi / 2.0`
# in obstacle_map.py) — those are intentionally NOT listed below; they are
# real findings, not false positives, and should stay failing until fixed.

# --- CHECK A: net_classification.py pattern-set constants ------------------
# These frozensets (GROUND_NET_PATTERNS, POWER_NET_PATTERNS, etc.) are NOT
# runtime parameters threaded into a Rust call — the Rust classifiers
# (`_rs.is_ground_net(name)` etc.) take only `name` and hard-code the same
# literal pattern sets internally. The Python constants exist so
# `tests/wave4_phase2/test_core_contracts_differential.py` can cross-check
# `oracle.GROUND_NET_PATTERNS` (etc.) against the Rust predicates'
# behaviour independently — i.e. there IS a differential guard here, just
# not a call-site argument. Confirmed by reading net_classification.py and
# its differential test; no call site exists where these could be threaded
# through as an argument in the first place.
CHECK_A|packages/temper-io-types/src/placer_core/netclass.rs|GROUND_NET_PATTERNS|packages/temper-placer/src/temper_placer/core/net_classification.py  # reason: pattern-set constant hard-coded identically in the Rust classifier, not a threadable per-call parameter; cross-checked by test_core_contracts_differential.py.
CHECK_A|packages/temper-io-types/src/placer_core/netclass.rs|POWER_NET_PATTERNS|packages/temper-placer/src/temper_placer/core/net_classification.py  # reason: same as GROUND_NET_PATTERNS above — hard-coded pattern set, not a call-site parameter, cross-checked by test_core_contracts_differential.py.
